\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RClauseformation2
< m1:I1::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec1}
                  [ mu1,
                    predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu2],
                    mu3
                  ]
>

< m :I2::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
               [ mu1, 
                 predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                        [ auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}
			      [ head/SUBVERB{SUBVERBrec1}
				    [ head/BVERB(AUX_serbverbkey){BVERBrec1}
				    ]
			      ],
                           mu2
                        ],
                 mu3
               ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: VERBPPROPrec1.voice = passive
       I2: CLAUSErec1.voice = passive
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: CLAUSErec1 := COPYT_verbpproptoclause(VERBPPROPrec1);
               (* all other attributes retain the default values *)
              SUBVERBrec1 := COPYT_btosubverb(BVERBrec1);
              VERBrec1 := COPYT_subtoverb(SUBVERBrec1)
                (* other attributes retain their default values *)
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: ( CLAUSErec1 =
	        { 
		 mood        : omegamood
		 aspecto     : omegaaspecto  
		 tiempo      : omegatiempo 
		 retro       : false       
		 finiteness  : omegafin
	        }
              )
              (* the default values for these attributes *) AND
              ( VERBrec1 = COPYT_subtoverb(SUBVERBrec1) ) AND
              ( SUBVERBrec1 = COPYT_btosubverb(BVERBrec1) )
          A1: VERBPPROPrec1 := COPYT_clausetoverbpprop(CLAUSErec1)
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RClauseformation2
\item[* relevant examples:] batido x2 por x1 $\rightarrow$ \\
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  \ \ \ {\em} ser batido x2 por x1
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] xpproptoclause
\item[* class:] RC:Clauseformation
\item[* date of creation:] 18-DEC-1987
\item[* author:] Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] RC_Clauseformation, Dutch, Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 04/02/87\ \ \ \ \ author: Jan Odijk\\
After consultation with Lisette Appelo it has been decided to put the auxiliary
inside the VERBP instead of outside of the VERBP. This is more convenient,
since it is not easy (impossible) to abstract over difference in depth in a
S-tree. 
\item date: 08/02/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster \\
The VERB within VERBPPROP doesn't have to be assigned "modo = PtcPas" anymore, 
since this has been done in the Voicerules.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Make a CLAUSE from a VERBPPROP with passive voice. Insert the 
auxiliary ser. (The main verb has been assigned the modus past participle 
already in the Voicerules).
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
